255
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,280
Uh... Mom, where's Dad?

256
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:21,580
Who? Uh, tall guy, nice smile, looks like a talk show host.

257
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:26,580
Oh, him? Uh, he's at the movies.

258
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:35,320
Fight. Hi, boys.

259
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:36,420
Mother home yet?

260
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,880
Uh, blonde woman?

261
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:39,900
Looks like Donna DeVarona.

262
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:43,580
Yeah, that's her.

263
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:47,760
Upstairs. Great. That's great.

264
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:48,980
Okay, good night, boys.

265
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:52,700
Wow, he didn't send me to bed either.

266
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:55,000
What do you say we go for a doubleheader?

267
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:57,120
No, I think I'll turn in.

268
00:13:58,920 --> 00:13:59,800
Steve, I like you!

269
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:13,500
I'm sorry. Taxi.

270
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:22,540
Oh. Maggie, anger is not something that should be left inside to seethe and fester.

271
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:27,400
Jason, you make our marriage sound like a boil that needs lancing.

272
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:30,340
Okay, that's good.

273
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,240
Come on, go with that.

274
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:36,120
Jason, I'd rather not talk about this right now because I might say or do something

275
