It is usually how they really feel.

326
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,660
Oh. Nuts! See?

327
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,920
Do you know, I don't see any point in continuing this.

328
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:12,460
Do you see any point in continuing this?

329
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,100
No, I don't.

330
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:16,640
Well, I just think that the way you're acting tonight, Maggie, I don't even know

331
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:18,300
you. Well, that's exactly how I feel!

332
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,480
Oh, well, blurt, blurt.

333
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,260
I'm sorry. Ben, I cannot sit here and watch you eat that for breakfast.

334
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:45,620
So close your eyes.

335
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,840
Do you guys have any idea what's going on?

336
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,660
You are not gonna believe this.

337
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:54,180
Mom and Dad are fighting.

338
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:56,800
How'd you know?

339
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:01,200
Well, first, Dad slept on the couch, and second, he didn't just dress up to go

340
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,200
jogging. He actually went.

341
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:07,940
Not only that, Mom actually said we should get our own breakfast.

342
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:11,420
Well, we've got to do something about this.

343
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:16,840
Why? Mike, this is Mom and Dad we're talking about.

344
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:19,640
I mean, at their age, somebody has to look out for them.

345
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:25,560
True. Yeah, I think we should clear this thing up before Ben becomes a total porker.

346
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:29,000
Hey, I'm making the best out of a bad situation.

347
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:31,780
I know what would work.

348
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,880
I mean, they couldn't be mad at each other if one of their kids were in trouble,

349
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:37,020
right? No, no, no, no, no.

350
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:38,880
Carol, I'm always in trouble.

351
